Fault Module Files

friction_fault.py
Purpose: Simulates mechanical friction in reaction wheels
•	Physical Model: 
o	Increases Coulomb friction coefficient
o	Temperature rise calculation
o	Power loss estimation
•	Implementation: 
o	Uses BSK_Dynamics wheel friction model
o	Calculates cumulative energy loss
o	Tracks temperature evolution
•	Outputs: 
o	Wheel speed degradation plots
o	Temperature evolution graphs
o	Power consumption analysis

powerlimit_fault.py
Purpose: Simulates power system constraints
•	Physical Model: 
o	Limits maximum motor torque
o	Models power saturation effects
o	Implements backup wheel activation
•	Implementation: 
o	Modifies maxMotorTorque parameter
o	Phased simulation approach
o	RW4 activation after delay
•	Outputs: 
o	Power consumption plots
o	Control effectiveness analysis
o	Energy conservation metrics

encoder_fault.py
Purpose: Simulates sensor measurement errors
•	Physical Model: 
o	Introduces measurement bias/noise
o	Creates control loop instability
o	Models feedback corruption
•	Implementation: 
o	Modifies wheel speed feedback
o	Increases effective friction
o	Generates control oscillations
•	Outputs: 
o	Control torque oscillations
o	Attitude error growth
o	RMS control effort analysis

battery_fault.py
Purpose: Simulates battery degradation and power system failures
•	Physical Model: 
o	Increased power consumption
o	Battery state-of-charge tracking
o	Safe mode triggering
•	Implementation: 
o	SimpleBattery module integration
o	Power sink fault injection
o	Solar panel modeling
•	Outputs: 
o	Battery discharge curves
o	Power balance analysis
o	Safe mode activation timing

